WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.210
Amplifier Agent is the easy way
to bring AI into your product,

2
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.940
with some really cool features,
as well as all the things you would expect.

3
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.330
You shouldn't have
to study a new framework.

4
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.060
We do the agent engineering.
Your focus can remain on the experience.

5
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.500
Let's look at one example
of how you could use it.

6
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.830
Say you're building an app
for football coaches

7
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.620
where you want the insights generated
consistently and over large amounts of data.

8
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.780
First, ask your agent to use
Amplifier Agent for the intelligence layer.

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.460
It's built to make that integration easy.

10
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.490
Then your app hands Amplifier Agent
a task and your expertise,

11
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.160
and takes it from there.

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.340
Let's go through an example
of how Amplifier Agent will work.

13
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.560
Say you want to analyze every
game from the last five seasons.

14
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.740
It is designed to break up that work
into smaller, more manageable tasks.

15
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.580
It will run for hours and stay on track,
finding all the patterns.

16
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.500
This amount of work does
not have to mean a big bill.

17
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.210
Fast, low-cost models chart
each game at the same time,

18
00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.600
and a stronger model can
connect the patterns.

19
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.350
And when a piece needs a specialist,

20
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.000
it can hand it to a Smart Tool.

21
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.230
They are the know-how that is packaged once,
with their own intelligence,

22
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.900
so that you get consistent
benefits from it.

23
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.460
Also, an agent should not be a black box.

24
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.670
Every run ends up in Context Intelligence,

25
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.300
so that you can see what it did
and how to improve for next time.

26
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.490
Finally, it has all the pieces you expect.

27
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.170
It works with the model you already use,
any major provider,

28
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.030
your Copilot, your ChatGPT subscription,

29
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.000
or a model on your own machine.

30
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.460
It has multiple surfaces
and it's open source.

31
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.030
To get started, ask your coding agent
to install the Amplifier Agent skill,

32
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.920
then tell it what you're building.
